12967	/// Outcome of one generated case: the generator decides acceptance from the
12968	/// candidate itself, so `accepted`/`discards` are MEASURED, never assumed.
12969	enum Case {
12970	    /// In-domain and every metamorphic relation held. Carries a WITNESS of what
12971	    /// the code under test actually produced for this input.
12972	    ///
12973	    /// The witness exists because of M17.5 pass-2 #16. The evidence digest used
12974	    /// to absorb only the generator's RNG state, which made it a fingerprint of
12975	    /// the GENERATOR and provably independent of the code being tested: delete
12976	    /// every `ensure!` in every case function below and, so long as the number
12977	    /// of RNG draws is unchanged, the recorded `evidence_hash` is bit-identical.
12978	    /// Two different formatters would hash the same. A hash that cannot
12979	    /// distinguish the implementation from a no-op is not evidence about the
12980	    /// implementation.
12981	    ///
12982	    /// So each family now returns bytes derived from the output it observed, and
12983	    /// the runner folds those into the digest. An empty witness is refused.
12984	    Accepted {
12985	        category: &'static str,
12986	        witness: Vec<u8>,
12987	    },
12988	    /// Out of the declared domain; not evidence either way.
12989	    /// Out of domain, or a relation that legitimately does not apply. Carries
12990	    /// a WITNESS of WHY, for the same reason `Accepted` does (M17.5 F-30).
12991	    ///
12992	    /// The runner used to record a discard as the single byte `b"D"`, so the
12993	    /// digest absorbed the COUNT of discards and nothing about them. Six
12994	    /// mutants inside `case_repair`'s cycle construction survived on exactly
12995	    /// that: each kept the plan cyclic, so each still discarded, and the
12996	    /// evidence could not tell the shapes apart. ADR-0020 §4 says attempts and
12997	    /// discards are RECORDED; counting is not recording.
12998	    Discarded {
12999	        category: &'static str,
13000	        witness: Vec<u8>,
13001	    },
13002	    /// Declared negative input. Unlike a discard, this case is part of the
13003	    /// exercised input domain and remains visible in campaign accounting.
13004	    Negative {
13005	        category: &'static str,
13006	        witness: Vec<u8>,
13007	    },
13008	}
