 3889	/// A mutant claiming `killed` must be killed by a test that CAN RUN
 3890	/// (M17.5 F-27 / P1-A02, F-28).
 3891	///
 3892	/// ADR-0020 §4 wants at least 64 semantic mutants at a 100% kill rate. The
 3893	/// packet declares 65, each naming the tests that would catch it — and as of
 3894	/// 2026-08-03 **not one of those 35 distinct tests is runnable**: 27 exist only
 3895	/// as strings in the packet (M18–M24 have not been authorized, so
 3896	/// `conformance/tests/milestones/` has no m18..m24 at all), and the remaining 8
 3897	/// exist but are `#[ignore]`d under the AM-17.2 Phase 1 quarantine.
 3898	///
 3899	/// A kill demonstrated by a test that does not exist is not demonstrated. A
 3900	/// kill demonstrated by a test nobody runs is not demonstrated either — an
 3901	/// `#[ignore]`d test cannot fail, so it cannot witness anything.
 3902	///
 3903	/// This check exists so that gap cannot be closed by editing dispositions to
 3904	/// `killed`. It is deliberately unsatisfiable today, and that is the correct
 3905	/// state: the mutation requirement is GATED on the Phase 1 milestones writing
 3906	/// their tests, not on anything M17.5 can produce.
 3907	/// How each mutation operator is observed. AM-17.10: a killer is derived, not
 3908	/// declared, and the primary killer is the test whose evidence kind is the way
 3909	/// this operator's defect shows itself. Closed table — a new operator must
 3910	/// name its observation here before the plan can carry it.
 3911	const MUTANT_OBSERVATION_KIND: [(&str, &str); 13] = [
 3912	    ("broadened-allow-list", "negative"),
 3913	    ("disabled-crash-point", "recovery"),
 3914	    ("missing-enum-dispatch", "malformed"),
 3915	    ("oracle-short-circuit", "positive"),
 3916	    ("ordering-nondeterminism", "replay"),
 3917	    ("predicate-deletion", "positive"),
 3918	    ("predicate-inversion", "negative"),
 3919	    ("skipped-durable-transition", "recovery"),
 3920	    ("stale-basis-acceptance", "basis"),
 3921	    ("success-error-substitution", "negative"),
 3922	    ("threshold-minus-one", "malformed"),
 3923	    ("threshold-plus-one", "malformed"),
 3924	    ("wrong-holder-selection", "basis"),
 3925	];
