 9659	/// The lines a wrong-holder mutation can redirect. Blind pass 1 at `ec045588`
 9660	/// (A05): `self.store.begin()?` reads a member off a receiver exactly as
 9661	/// `inner.state.nodes.get(&id)` does, and one is the only store there is while
 9662	/// the other has a sibling to be redirected to. Nothing in the text says
 9663	/// which, so this operator's reach is not lexically decidable, and pretending
 9664	/// otherwise is how P1-M047 came to declare a mutation no patch could
 9665	/// implement. The set is closed and shared with
 9666	/// `verify_mutant_operator_patch`: one statement of where the operator
 9667	/// applies, not two that can drift.
 9668	const WRONG_HOLDER_ANCHORS: [&str; 2] = [
 9669	    "&self.basis",
 9670	    "return Ok(inner.state.nodes.get(&id).cloned());",
 9671	];
