11020	/// Durable-transition call sites in tracked runtime source, by path.
11021	///
11022	/// Markers are call-shaped for the reason F-34 established for the
11023	/// `skipped-durable-transition` operator: a durable transition is a CALL, and
11024	/// matching bare words lets a rename satisfy the check.
11025	///
11026	/// Enumerated from `git ls-files`, never the filesystem (F-32): a scan that
11027	/// reads the working directory reports a different durable surface on a dirty
11028	/// tree than a fresh clone does, and the clone is the one that has to reproduce
11029	/// this.
11030	///
11031	/// `liminal-xtask` is excluded — the verifier is not runtime code, and its
11032	/// operator table contains the marker as a string literal, so including it
11033	/// would make this count self-referential. `tests/` is excluded: an integration
11034	/// test's commit is not a transition the product performs.
11035	///
11036	/// This is a TRIPWIRE, not a semantic census. It counts call sites textually,
11037	/// including any inside `#[cfg(test)]` modules, and its only job is to fail
11038	/// loudly when the durable surface moves under a disclosure that claims to have
11039	/// surveyed it.
11040	///
11041	/// Known imprecision, and its direction: line comments (`//`, and `///` with
11042	/// them) are skipped, but a marker inside a block comment or a string literal
11043	/// still counts. That errs toward REJECTION — a spurious match fails a packet
11044	/// that was honest, which a human then corrects. The opposite error, silently
11045	/// undercounting, would let a real durable transition hide, so the bias is the
11046	/// one worth having.
11047	/// How many times `line` names one of `symbols` as a durable transition.
11048	///
11049	/// Blind pass 1 at 5fb1b57 (A05): matching `symbol(` missed a turbofish
11050	/// (`rename::<T>(`) and a function pointer (`let f = fs::rename;`). The symbol
11051	/// is matched on a word boundary and accepted when what follows is a call, a
11052	/// path or turbofish, or the end of a value — never when it is more
11053	/// identifier, so `rename_all` and `append_str` are not renames and appends.
11054	/// Counting occurrences rather than marker spellings keeps one call site worth
11055	/// one site however many spellings would match it.
11056	fn durable_symbol_hits(line: &str, symbols: &[String]) -> usize {
11057	    let identifier = |ch: char| ch.is_alphanumeric() || ch == '_';
11058	    let mut hits = 0;
11059	    for symbol in symbols {
11060	        for (offset, _) in line.match_indices(symbol.as_str()) {
11061	            if line[..offset].chars().next_back().is_some_and(identifier) {
11062	                continue;
11063	            }
11064	            let rest = &line[offset + symbol.len()..];
11065	            let follows = rest.starts_with('(')
11066	                || rest.starts_with("::")
11067	                || rest.starts_with(';')
11068	                || rest.starts_with(',')
11069	                || rest.starts_with(')');
11070	            if follows {
11071	                hits += 1;
11072	            }
11073	        }
11074	    }
11075	    hits
11076	}
